# Gradle ships gradlew.bat with CRLF line endings, as a Windows batch file must have.
# Without this, git's whitespace check reads each carriage return as a trailing space and
# reports every changed line as an error. That is not cosmetic here: the version-port
# packager runs `git diff --cached --check` over the staged port, so a wrapper bump makes
# every release-branch port abort before it can be validated or published.
#
# `cr-at-eol` adds to git's default rules rather than replacing them, so genuine trailing
# whitespace before the carriage return is still reported.
*.bat whitespace=cr-at-eol

# mod-base manages the files below: `template check` compares the managed ones (the caller's
# managed region included) byte for byte with the kit's template and reads the others line by
# line. Git for Windows' default `core.autocrlf=true` would check them out with CRLF line endings
# and fail that check on a clean clone, so they are always checked out with LF, whatever the local
# setting. The list is exactly the template manifest's managed and fragment paths.
/.gitattributes text eol=lf
/.gitignore text eol=lf
/.github/CODEOWNERS text eol=lf
/.github/dependabot.yml text eol=lf
/.github/pull_request_template.md text eol=lf
/.github/workflows/pages.yml text eol=lf
/AGENTS.md text eol=lf
/docs/ai/shared/PUBLIC-EVIDENCE.md text eol=lf
/docs/ai/shared/REPOSITORY.md text eol=lf
/scripts/ci/mod_base_kit.py text eol=lf
